# macOS-Specific Guidelines

**Identity, architecture, forbidden patterns:** hexpal-project.mdc.

## Permissions
- HEXPal requires zero system permissions — color picking uses NSColorSampler, hotkey uses KeyboardShortcuts (no entitlements needed)

## Menu Bar App Best Practices
- No dock icon (LSUIElement = true)
- Menu bar icon should be minimal and recognizable
- Respect macOS design guidelines
- Support dark mode

## Color Picking
- Use NSColorSampler exclusively — Apple's system API handles all color sampling internally
- NSColorSampler provides its own magnifier loupe and requires no permissions
- Convert NSColor to sRGB for accurate HEX representation

## Global Hotkeys
- Use KeyboardShortcuts package (Carbon RegisterEventHotKey) — App Store approved, no Accessibility required
- Default: Cmd+Shift+P (customizable)
- Handle conflicts gracefully
- Provide alternative activation via menu bar click

## UI/UX Guidelines
- Minimal and clean design
- Fast and responsive
- Intuitive and discoverable
- Consistent with macOS design
- Follow macOS Human Interface Guidelines

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)
**Full requirements:** hexpal-project.mdc. HexPal must be 100% WCAG 2.2 AA accessible.

- **SwiftUI:** Use `.accessibilityLabel()`, `.accessibilityHint()`, `.accessibilityValue()`, `.accessibilityAddTraits()` on every interactive view. Use `.accessibilityHidden(true)` only for purely decorative elements.
- **AppKit:** Set `accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityHint`, `accessibilityRole` on NSView/NSControl subclasses.
- **Menu bar items:** Provide accessibility labels for the status item and menu items.
- **Keyboard:** All actions reachable via keyboard. Support Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, Escape.
- **VoiceOver:** Test every new view with Cmd+F5. Announce picked color (HEX value) and contrast results clearly.
- **Contrast:** App chrome (buttons, text, backgrounds) must meet 4.5:1 (text) or 3:1 (large) — use the app's contrast checker on app UI colors.

## Critical Error Handling
- Hotkey registration failures: Check for key conflicts, provide fallback (menu bar click)
- Memory issues: Monitor memory usage, optimize caching strategies
